@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Equipment connections
+
+Serve the homepage over HTTPS in production. No backend proxy or device discovery is used: both cards make a direct browser GET to the entered URL, only after Connect is selected. The defaults are examples; replace them with the equipment's actual status endpoints. No brewing command is sent.
+
+- Brewer default: `http://192.168.1.100/api/status` on the shop's private LAN.
+- Desktop helper default: `http://127.0.0.1:45678/health` on the visitor's own computer.
+- The endpoint must return a 2xx status and standard CORS headers allowing the homepage's origin (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin`). No credentials are sent and no response body format is required.
+- Browser permissions are queried separately as `local-network` and `loopback-network`; unsupported permission queries fall back to explicit user-initiated requests. Fetch declares the corresponding `targetAddressSpace`. Local HTTP support varies by browser; use a compatible browser or a trusted HTTPS endpoint. No deprecated PNA preflight headers are added.
+- Status is a one-time reachability check, not a persistent session or live brew status. Disconnect cancels an in-flight request or clears the last check; it does not stop the device. Browser permission revocation clears the card's status.
+- Requests time out after 30 seconds, omit credentials and referrers, bypass caches, and reject redirects. Addresses are restricted to the card's intended private LAN or loopback space. Addresses are not persisted.
+
+Run automated checks with `node --test tests/connections.test.mjs`. This static project has no build script.
